# MyTimetable Implementation Plan

## 1. Class Design & Architecture
* **Encapsulation & Visibility**: Set all instance variables to `private` or `protected`. Use getters/setters only where necessary.
* **Inheritance & Hierarchy**: Use superclass methods to manipulate superclass properties from within subclasses without direct attribute access.
  * `Course` (Superclass): Stores course name, capacity, year, delivery mode, day of lecture, time of lecture, duration, and number of current enrolments.
  * `FaceToFaceCourse` (Subclass): Handles capacity limits and max-capacity enrolment checks.
  * `OnlineCourse` (Subclass): Handles delivery with no capacity constraint (`Capacity` = `N/A`).
* **Collections**: Use Java Collections Framework (JCF) structures (e.g., `ArrayList`, `List`) to store all courses and enrolled courses. No normal arrays.

